---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/layout/Section.astro";
import Container from "../components/layout/Container.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
import ClassifiedBand from "../components/ui/ClassifiedBand.astro";
import PitchDeckNav from "../components/ui/PitchDeckNav.astro";
import CTA from "../components/ui/CTA.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/typography/Eyebrow.astro";
import Heading from "../components/typography/Heading.astro";
import Rule from "../components/typography/Rule.astro";
import "@/styles/global.css";
---

<Layout title="MI5 Executive Briefing — Cultural Soft-Power vs. Imperial Prestige">
  <ClassifiedBand label="TOP SECRET — MI5 EXECUTIVE BRIEFING // FINAL STATEMENT" />

  <!-- ─── PAGE HEADER ─── -->
  <Section variant="black" spacing="sm">
    <Container>
      <Eyebrow>Final Thoughts</Eyebrow>
      <Heading level={2} variant="section">The <em>Ultimate Cosmic Joke</em></Heading>
      <Rule />
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── ULTIMATE COSMIC JOKE ─── -->
  <Section variant="paper" spacing="lg">
    <Container>
      <!-- Visual Description -->
      <div class="visual-description">
        <img src="/falklands-office.jpg" alt="Bleak wide shot of Falklands office with two tiny grey desks under harsh fluorescent lights" class="bleak-shot" />
        <p class="image-caption">The final visual beat: Nigel and Clive in exile</p>
      </div>

      <div class="closing-statement">
        <p class="prose">
          The ultimate irony of <em>Her Majesty’s Displeasure</em> is that the entire
          multi-year, multi-million pound covert operation—the surveillance,
          the psychological warfare, the administrative sabotage, even the
          contemplated assassination—was rendered utterly meaningless by a
          single, deranged fan with a cheap pistol in New York City.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          While the Crown and MI5 were busy treating John Lennon as a
          existential threat to the realm, Mark David Chapman was preparing to
          prove that all that machinery, all that paranoia, all that effort was
          irrelevant. The state could not kill Lennon’s legacy; only a
          meaningless act of violence could do that. And in the end, the
          system’s greatest failure wasn’t that it almost murdered a
          musician—it’s that it spent years and vast resources trying to
          solve a problem that was never really about them at all.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          The series concludes not with a bang, but with a quiet, devastating
          shrug. The ultimate cosmic joke is that the powerful are never as
          powerful as they think, the threats are never as controllable as
          they believe, and the entire grand machinery of state can be
          rendered obsolete by a single, random act that no amount of
          surveillance or sabotage could ever prevent.
        </p>

        <!-- Additional Content -->
        <div class="additional-content">
          <p class="prose">
            At its core, <em>Her Majesty’s Displeasure</em> is a tragedy dressed up as a brilliant workplace comedy. It is an exploration of the absolute futility of institutional control when faced with the unpredictable, volcanic power of human art and culture.
          </p>
          <p class="prose">
            The show intentionally ends not in the roaring, glamorous rock-and-roll haze of London or New York, but in a tiny, frozen, forgotten administrative outpost in the Falkland Islands. When Nigel and Clive hear that a lone, deranged fan has killed John Lennon, the silence that falls over their identical desks is the emotional weight of the entire series.
          </p>
          <p class="prose">
            We are leaving the audience with an unforgettable, existential punchline: that the vast, calculation-heavy, multi-million dollar machinery of the British Empire spent five grueling years trying and failing to break an artist's spirit—only to watch a random nobody achieve it in a single afternoon for absolutely nothing. It is a story about the systems we build, the pensions we chase, and the beautiful, tragic chaos that completely ignores them both.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── NAVIGATION ─── -->
  <PitchDeckNav current="/closing" />

  <!-- ─── FOOTER ─── -->
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .visual-description {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .bleak-shot {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 400px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    filter: grayscale(100%) contrast(1.1);
  }

  .image-caption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05rem;
  }

  .closing-statement p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .closing-statement p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .additional-content {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border-soft);
  }
</style>